# Instance configuration, written by Cheshire Cat and edited from its admin
# panel: it belongs to the installation, not to the plugin. The core recreates
# it from the defaults in settings.py the first time the plugin is activated.
#
# It matters more here than in an ordinary plugin: this is where the Uptime Kuma
# instance URL, the status page slug and — if the admin field is used instead of
# the environment variable — the push token end up.
#
# Anchored to the repository root, so a settings.json elsewhere stays visible.
/settings.json
